{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019bUBQnGzi9sqEgDBwz6LDK","type":"tool_result","content":"# Controllers\n\nEach file here exports a class whose public methods are dispatcher\n**actions**. `src/renderer/main.js` builds a flat map of action name ->\nhandler, and `lib/dispatcher.js` looks actions up **by string name** at\ncall time.\n\nConsequences when editing a controller:\n\n- Never delete a public method just because its body became empty.\n  Callers dispatch by name from JSX (`onClick={() => dispatch('foo')}`)\n  and from the main process\n  (`windows.main.dispatch('uncaughtError', ...)`), so a missing method\n  is a runtime lookup failure, not a compile error. Leave an empty\n  method with a comment instead.\n- Renaming a method means grepping for the string, not for the\n  identifier. Check `src/renderer/pages/`, `src/renderer/components/`\n  and `src/main/` too.\n- Controllers are lazily *constructed* via `fn-getter` in `main.js`, but\n  since the ESM conversion they are no longer lazily *loaded* -- their\n  `import` in `main.js` is hoisted, so every module-level import here is\n  paid at startup. A heavy new dependency in a controller now costs\n  startup time. There is no synchronous ESM equivalent of the old lazy\n  `require`, so if that ever matters the fix is a bundler-level split,\n  not an inner `require`.\n\n**A controller under unit test is compiled by the test itself.**\n`build:node` ignores `controllers/`, so there is no Babel output for\n`test/unit/*.js` to require (ADR-010); the three call-site files\n(`os-ipc-call-sites.js`, `engine-ipc-call-sites.js`,\n      81 src/renderer/controllers/AGENTS.md\n     211 src/AGENTS.md\n     292 total","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f68062db-8b20-4413-9a9d-110c293d5a53","uuid":"2749c24e-8dac-4836-842a-3f0a6c340d63","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:13:11.911Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Controllers\n\nEach file here exports a class whose public methods are dispatcher\n**actions**. `src/renderer/main.js` builds a flat map of action name ->\nhandler, and `lib/dispatcher.js` looks actions up **by string name** at\ncall time.\n\nConsequences when editing a controller:\n\n- Never delete a public method just because its body became empty.\n  Callers dispatch by name from JSX (`onClick={() => dispatch('foo')}`)\n  and from the main process\n  (`windows.main.dispatch('uncaughtError', ...)`), so a missing method\n  is a runtime lookup failure, not a compile error. Leave an empty\n  method with a comment instead.\n- Renaming a method means grepping for the string, not for the\n  identifier. Check `src/renderer/pages/`, `src/renderer/components/`\n  and `src/main/` too.\n- Controllers are lazily *constructed* via `fn-getter` in `main.js`, but\n  since the ESM conversion they are no longer lazily *loaded* -- their\n  `import` in `main.js` is hoisted, so every module-level import here is\n  paid at startup. A heavy new dependency in a controller now costs\n  startup time. There is no synchronous ESM equivalent of the old lazy\n  `require`, so if that ever matters the fix is a bundler-level split,\n  not an inner `require`.\n\n**A controller under unit test is compiled by the test itself.**\n`build:node` ignores `controllers/`, so there is no Babel output for\n`test/unit/*.js` to require (ADR-010); the three call-site files\n(`os-ipc-call-sites.js`, `engine-ipc-call-sites.js`,\n      81 src/renderer/controllers/AGENTS.md\n     211 src/AGENTS.md\n     292 total","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019bUBQnGzi9sqEgDBwz6LDK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8pDUHzyk8M1xT2s9Zsp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XbWhFjqYVQ2Q1kLgG9neHB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/webtorrent-desktop.memory-leaks-10-error-list-stays-bounded; cat >> src/renderer/controllers/AGENTS.md <<'EOF'\n\n**Record user-facing errors with `recordError` from\n`lib/error-list.js`**, never `state.errors.push(...)`. It drops errors\nolder than the banner window (`ERROR_WINDOW_MS`, which `pages/app.js`\nuses to filter) so the list stays bounded. `test/unit/error-list.js`\nscans `src/renderer/` and fails on a direct push.\nEOF\ncat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 10: error list stays bounded\n\nImplemented:\n- `src/renderer/lib/error-list.js`: `ERROR_WINDOW_MS` (5000),\n  `isRecent(error, now)`, `recordError(errors, message, now?)`.\n  recordError prunes stale entries in place (same array, so\n  `state.errors` references stay valid), then pushes.\n- `main.js` onError and `cast-controller.js` raise use recordError.\n- `pages/app.js` banner filter uses `isRecent` (shared window).\n- `test/unit/error-list.js`: bounded-list, keeps-recent, same-array,\n  and a source scan of src/renderer for `.errors.push/unshift/splice(`.\n- AGENTS.md note in src/renderer/controllers.\n\nReading of criteria: \"bounded\" = at most window/interval + 1 entries\nwhen errors arrive at a steady rate over 60 s.\n\nGotcha: compiling only `src/renderer/lib` with babel leaves `build/`\nwithout `config`, breaking other tests; use `npm run build:node`.\nEOF\nnpm test > /tmp/et10.log 2>&1; echo exit $?; tail -6 /tmp/et10.log"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":809,"cache_read_input_tokens":59378,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":809},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f68062db-8b20-4413-9a9d-110c293d5a53","uuid":"de170eb4-bb4f-45b6-b950-e2e8b545bb2e","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:13:18.138Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8pDU2sfWT6GbWj5K1YA","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XbWhFjqYVQ2Q1kLgG9neHB":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/webtorrent-desktop.memory-leaks-10-error-list-stays-bounded; cat >> src/renderer/controllers/AGENTS.md <<'EOF'\n\n**Record user-facing errors with `recordError` from\n`lib/error-list.js`**, never `state.errors.push(...)`. It drops errors\nolder than the banner window (`ERROR_WINDOW_MS`, which `pages/app.js`\nuses to filter) so the list stays bounded. `test/unit/error-list.js`\nscans `src/renderer/` and fails on a direct push.\nEOF\ncat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 10: error list stays bounded\n\nImplemented:\n- `src/renderer/lib/error-list.js`: `ERROR_WINDOW_MS` (5000),\n  `isRecent(error, now)`, `recordError(errors, message, now?)`.\n  recordError prunes stale entries in place (same array, so\n  `state.errors` references stay valid), then pushes.\n- `main.js` onError and `cast-controller.js` raise use recordError.\n- `pages/app.js` banner filter uses `isRecent` (shared window).\n- `test/unit/error-list.js`: bounded-list, keeps-recent, same-array,\n  and a source scan of src/renderer for `.errors.push/unshift/splice(`.\n- AGENTS.md note in src/renderer/controllers.\n\nReading of criteria: \"bounded\" = at most window/interval + 1 entries\nwhen errors arrive at a steady rate over 60 s.\n\nGotcha: compiling only `src/renderer/lib` with babel leaves `build/`\nwithout `config`, breaking other tests; use `npm run build:node`.\nEOF\nnpm test > /tmp/et10.log 2>&1; echo exit $?; tail -6 /tmp/et10.log"}}}
