{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8pFvVQVQmRh47mQbXzW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The error list now stays bounded. The full `npm test` run (lint, depcheck, build and all 4261 unit tests) passes, and everything is committed except the notes file.\n\n**What changed:**\n1. `src/renderer/lib/error-list.js` is a new module. It shares the 5000 ms banner window as `ERROR_WINDOW_MS`, and it adds `recordError(errors, message, now?)`. Each time `recordError` records an error, it first drops any older than the window. It edits the existing array rather than replacing it, so anything already pointing at `state.errors` stays valid.\n2. Both places that used to push errors directly now call `recordError`: `onError` in `src/renderer/main.js` and `raise` in `src/renderer/controllers/cast-controller.js`.\n3. The banner in `src/renderer/pages/app.js` now uses the shared window instead of its own hardcoded 5000, so it shows the same recent errors as before.\n4. `test/unit/error-list.js` covers the ticket's three checks:\n   - a steady stream of errors over 60 seconds keeps the list at about one window's worth;\n   - errors inside the window are kept;\n   - a scan of `src/renderer/` finds no direct `.errors.push`, `unshift` or `splice`.\n\n   It also checks that the array is edited in place. Every test failed before the code that makes it pass was written.\n5. I added a note to `src/renderer/controllers/AGENTS.md` telling future work to use `recordError`, never a direct push.\n\n[x] Recording many errors over a span longer than the banner window keeps the list bounded\n[x] Errors recorded within the banner window are kept\n[x] No site pushes to `state.errors` directly (source scan)\n\n**One gotcha, recorded in `.nightralph/notes.md`:** while iterating, compiling only `src/renderer/lib` left `build/` incomplete, and other test files failed on a missing `config` module. Running `npm run build:node` fixes it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":215,"cache_read_input_tokens":60920,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":215},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f68062db-8b20-4413-9a9d-110c293d5a53","uuid":"c9efe4fd-ef24-4e77-9bd2-43339b1d50c6","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:13:51.564Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8pFvCnY6EBx5JvGy6Rf"}
